  "implemented": [
    "The actual descriptor-free controller publishes and fsyncs its source/plan/identity/clock origin before Popen, without a future producer PID. Actual spawn and durable producer release then bind real PID/birth to that same origin.",
    "Each role validates the same hostname, public boot identifier and monotonic-clock domain. All version/capture/child-release/work waits use the original absolute work deadline; no new180-second or per-tool work window is granted.",
    "The controller starts one actual own-process total timer from the retained entry origin, waits only remaining total time and never adds300 or180 seconds. On an unfinished producer it writes inconclusive evidence and never sends TERM/KILL to the holder.",
    "OwnedToolScope accepts an optional diagnostic deadline. Work expiry refuses new tool starts. The first cleanup start retains at most60 seconds capped by total; TERM/KILL uses only positively owned handles and rechecks remaining time before signals.",
    "If kernel cleanup is unverified at expiry, scope writes inconclusive evidence, stops new tool/signal requests and retains custody while passively observing kernel closure. No completed-within-budget or admission claim is made. The descriptor is released only after actual closure.",
